{"team":"BAL","col":"#9E86FF","identity":"run-heavy","funnel":"pass-funnel","plays_pg":59.0,"adot":8.5,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>A Ground-First Machine</h2><p>The backfield runs through one man \u2014 <strong>Derrick Henry</strong> absorbs <strong>76% of the carries</strong> (league ~59%), a true bell-cow share that makes his rushing volume among the safest floors in the sport when the script cooperates.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>Few offenses are as committed to the run as BAL. Their pass rate over expected sits at <strong>-8%</strong> \u2014 well below the -2% norm \u2014 and it collapses to 30% once they're in front. The script writes itself: build a lead, then bludgeon.</p><p>Their run game attacks the perimeter \u2014 <strong>33% of carries hit the edge</strong> (league ~25%), an outside-zone lean that rewards speed backs and can boom for chunk gains.</p><p>By the numbers it's an efficient unit \u2014 a 48% success rate (above the 44% average).</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Their red-zone identity is <strong>run-first</strong> (43% pass), funnelling touchdown equity to <strong>Derrick Henry</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 They Force the Throw</h2><p><strong>Soft against opposing WR1s</strong> \u2014 74 rec yds/game (vs ~58). A rec-yards target.</p><p>They surrender <strong>94 rushing</strong> and <strong>257 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). They wall the run and force the throw \u2014 <strong>attack with the opposing WR room</strong>.</p><p><strong>Soft against backs out of the backfield</strong> \u2014 22 rec yds/game (vs ~18). A rec-yards target.</p><p>A stingy, efficient defense \u2014 just 42% success allowed (vs ~44%); temper expectations for opposing skill players.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: back <strong>Derrick Henry</strong>'s rushing volume in favored/positive scripts; <strong>opposing WR1/WR2</strong> are the target \u2014 this D forces the throw.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; t